  "notes": "{安堵|あんど} expresses the feeling of relief when worry or anxiety is lifted. It has a somewhat literary or formal tone.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to feel relieved (verb)\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧ + noun: relief + noun (attributive)\n{安堵|あんど} is often used in written Japanese, news, and formal speech rather than casual conversation.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{息|いき}→息：02176_iki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦つく→つく：noentry⟧: to breathe a sigh of relief\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{表情|ひょうじょう}→表情：03585_hyoujou⟧: relieved expression\n- ⟦{安堵感|あんどかん}→安堵感：19956_andokan⟧: feeling of relief\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{色|いろ}→色：00849_iro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{浮|う}かべる→浮かべる：13314_ukaberu⟧: to show relief (on one's face)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦ほっとする→ほっとする：07652_hottosuru⟧: to feel relieved (casual, everyday)\n- ⟦{安心|あんしん}する→安心する：06067_anshinsuru⟧: to feel at ease, relieved (neutral)\n- {安堵|あんど}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to feel relieved (literary, formal)",
